usage: runner_multi.py [-h] --commit COMMIT --jobs JOBS
                       [--boot-script {tools/colab_chat/boot_jobs.sh,tools/colab_chat/boot_commands.sh,tools/colab_chat/boot_commands_sparse.sh}]
                       [--max-hours MAX_HOURS] [--deadline-utc DEADLINE_UTC]
                       --name NAME --art ART --state-dir STATE_DIR
                       [--upload UPLOAD] [--backend {colab,runpod}]
                       [--gpu GPU] [--cloud {SECURE,COMMUNITY}]
                       [--volume-gb VOLUME_GB] [--datacenter DATACENTER]
                       [--image IMAGE] [--max-usd MAX_USD]

Reclaim-resilient Colab (or RunPod) driver for a session of several training
jobs.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --commit COMMIT
  --jobs JOBS           jobs JSON, path relative to the paperkiln repo root
  --boot-script {tools/colab_chat/boot_jobs.sh,tools/colab_chat/boot_commands.sh,tools/colab_chat/boot_commands_sparse.sh}
                        pinned VM boot; command-only boot skips trainer and
                        corpus setup
  --max-hours MAX_HOURS
  --deadline-utc DEADLINE_UTC
                        absolute timezone-aware ISO8601 ceiling, preserved
                        across watchdog restarts
  --name NAME           Colab session name (this run's own)
  --art ART             local artifact directory
  --state-dir STATE_DIR
                        runner state, pid file and log
  --upload UPLOAD       KEY=LOCAL_PATH, sent to /content/chat/upload/KEY
  --backend {colab,runpod}
  --gpu GPU             GPU type (both backends; L4 is the study GPU)
  --cloud {SECURE,COMMUNITY}
                        RunPod cloud
  --volume-gb VOLUME_GB
                        RunPod network volume size
  --datacenter DATACENTER
                        RunPod data centre (default: one with the GPU in
                        stock)
  --image IMAGE         RunPod image (default: runpod_transport.IMAGE)
  --max-usd MAX_USD     RunPod: stop and create nothing once this runner's
                        ledger passes this many dollars
